{"id": "G029", "service_id": "reporting-worker", "purl": "pkg:pypi/aiohttp@3.8.5", "vuln_id": "CVE-2026-54280", "aliases": ["GHSA-9x8q-7h8h-wcw9", "PYSEC-2026-2113"], "bucket": "range_conflict", "label": "not_affected", "hard": true, "fixed_in": null, "evidence": ["https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/a762eda5242f6490d6ba667533193f8b473ad587", "https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/blob/v3.8.5/aiohttp/payload.py"], "note": "The fix wraps Payload.close() in finally inside write_eof. 3.8.5 has no Payload.close() hook; its file payloads close the file in a finally inside write(), so a mid-body disconnect still releases it. NVD (>=3.12.1) is right; OSV/GHSA (from 0) are too broad.", "labelled_by": "claude-code", "labelled_at": "2026-10-25", "reviewed_by": null}
